            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mom2zz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the first cheeseball I have made, and it has received rave reviews. It makes a very large portion, so I now make two cheeseballs and freeze one. (You could also halve the recipe). I have found that the half portion is sufficient for any party.\r\n\r\nI modified the recipe a bit, using 1 cup Mexican blend cheese and skipping the pepper jack (didn't have it on hand). I also skipped the jalapenos, but added bacon and green onions. I doubled the Worcestershire sauce and rolled the cheeseball in the shredded cheese as the author suggested. The green peppers add great color and crunch.\r\n\r\nI highly recommend this recipe, it's easy and different. Thanks Anita!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Donna Lange"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this for the families Christmas get together. It was a hit! Added a little green onion and some extra pepper jack cheese. Shaped it like a tree and covered it in cilantro. Used some of the left overs as the cheese in a ham and cheese omelet. Outstanding.",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-26T06:30:19.843Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "amandak23k"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty!!! I cut the recipe down because I only wanted to use one 8oz package of cream cheese. I shredded half a brick of pepperjack cheese and added about that much of shredded cheddar cheese. I used a serrano pepper for more heat, very YUMMY! I just realized I left the worch. sauce out...",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-14T17:15:12.673Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "G Paul"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my first cheeseball to make. Following some suggestions from other reviews, I used a cup of pepper jack and a cup of cheddar cheeses. I used 2 jalapenos (next time I will leave the seeds in to pack some heat) I used about 2 tablespoons of worcestershire sauce, 2 teaspoons garlic powder, several drops of Louisiana hot sauce and a dash of lime juice. It turned out very well. I will definitely make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-20T12:07:24.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tracy Curtis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was a hit!! I added a little more cheese then was written down and also I minced 2 cloves of garlic into it instead of adding the garlic salt. I rolled the ball in cilantro and chopped walnuts. I made two cheese balls with this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-27T10:42:52.197Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LAM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great taste. Zesty!! Try adding one finely chopped green onion in place of half the jalapeno pepper. Crush in some garlic in place of garlic salt. If you don't have worcestershire, put in equal parts A-1 and soy sauce. Delicious!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-01-30T14:59:59.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "scarlett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Have passed this recipe on numerous times to family &amp; friends. I even get requests to make it. I mix mine and serve in a bowl which makes for easy clean-up. Keep in the fridge overnight before serving - the longer it rests, the better.",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-21T12:04:39.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KeysBum"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great cheese ball. The only change I made was that I rolled it in finely chopped walnuts. That's what my mom always did with her cheese balls when I was a kid. I just like the texture the nuts add. I also used sharp cheddar and let it sit in the frig overnight. A good quick cheese ball recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-06T16:48:50.340Z"
          },
          {
